[{:adr/consequences ["git demoted to terminal materialize layer; never sees 20 concurrent writers (conflict structurally eliminated)" "all agent turn-history/proposal/receipt land on append-only Datom log; resumable/auditable/time-travelable (kotoba-code as-of becomes fleet audit)" "layers on top of west/repos.edn/optimistic-single-entry-commit/murakumo without breaking them (back-compat)" "new single point is the governor, but it is split per-repo and isolated by lease, so failure is localized" "coordinator itself needs a new child repo + west entry + RAD identity (actor completion condition)"], :adr/west-integration "{:repos-edn \"remains the partition SSoT\", :change \"pin advance driven by governor draining accepted proposals via the single-entry commit canonical path (ADR-2606272237) instead of human/agent ad-hoc API calls\", :invariants-kept [\"gen-west-manifest.cljs --check canonical\" \"pin == repo HEAD\"], :principle \"do not break existing guardrails; add a queue one layer above\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["coordinate many Claude Code agents across multiple PCs without git conflict" "lift coordination from git shared-mutable ref to kotoba append-only Datom log" "achieve work exclusion via optimistic lease-claim datoms (409 retry), not a lock server" "serialize materialization to git through a per-repo single-writer governor (actor invariant reused)" "layer on top of west/repos.edn/optimistic-single-entry-commit/murakumo without breaking them"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-fleet-coordination", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba/README.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-code/README.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/murakumo/README.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/datom/README.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272237-manifest-workflow-single-entry-commit.edn"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2606302000-kotoba-fleet-agent-coordination", :adr/maturity "[{:stage :F0, :deliverable [\"work/lease/proposal/claim/receipt datom schema in datom-clj\" \"contract test\"], :status :next} {:stage :F1, :deliverable [\"claim loop: optimistic lease + TTL + crash re-lease\" \"single-PC 2-3 agent PoC\"], :status :after-f0} {:stage :F2, :deliverable [\"governor drain: proposal -> gate -> west single-entry commit -> receipt\" \"git single writer\"], :status :after-f1} {:stage :F3, :deliverable [\"worktree / WASM pod isolation integrated into kotoba-code runtime\"], :status :after-f2} {:stage :F4, :deliverable [\"murakumo fleet-view extension\" \"2 PC x ~20 agent rollout\" \"log IPNS/CID replication ops\"], :status :future}]", :adr/missing-piece "{:name \"kotoba-fleet (working name) coordinator\", :schema-add {:to \"datom-clj\", :attrs [:work/* :lease/* :proposal/* :claim/* :receipt/*]}, :loops [{:loop \"claim\", :side \"agent\", :steps [\"optimistic lease\" \"run kotoba-code\" \"append proposal\"]} {:loop \"governor-drain\", :side \"per-repo\", :steps [\"proposal\" \"gate\" \"west single-entry commit\" \"receipt\"]} {:loop \"fleet-view\", :side \"murakumo\", :steps [\"20 lease TTL\" \"progress\" \"crash re-lease\" \"1 view\"]}], :scaffold \"standard new-actor flow: ADR -> .cljc canonical -> child repo -> west entry -> RAD identity\"}", :adr/same-file-contention "{:default \"file-set lease; a given file held by at most one lease at a time\", :structured-assets \"append-only set-union natural merge (EDN/datom)\", :code-text \"serialize via lease; optimistic claim race -> 409 -> reassign to other work\", :forbidden \"no silent last-writer-wins applied to code\"}", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-30", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606302000: kotoba Datom log を調整基板にした 20-agent fleet 並行開発\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-06-30\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\n現状は west manifest（`repos.edn` を SSoT に ~50 child repo へ partition）+ radicle +\nGitHub で、分散的に git 管理している。目標は **2 台の PC で計 ~20 個の terminal agent\n（Claude Code）を開き、並列・並行に開発しつつ conflict を出さない**こと。\n\ngit で conflict が出るのは「並列だから」ではなく、**共有可変 ref（`main`）に対する\n行ベース 3-way merge** という git の構造に起因する。20 agent が単一 `main` を奪い合うと\nロック競合 + テキスト merge marker になる。west で repo を割ったのは正しい第一歩だが、\n**調整(coordination)がまだ git の上にある**のが限界。\n\n一方、基盤はすでに揃っている:\n\n- **kotoba** — content-addressed distributed Datalog（Datom[CID/T] × EAVT × CACAO）。\n  1 actor = 1 Ed25519 鍵 = 鍵由来 IPNS graph、depth-1 自己 mint（CLAUDE.md）。\n- **kotoba-code** — model-neutral agentic coding agent。全 turn-history を Datom log に\n  as-of で積む＝**resumable / auditable / fleet-shared checkpointer**。\n- **murakumo** — Mac fleet の kotoba WASM mesh control plane。Tailscale/DID で全ノードを\n  1 view に畳む。durable outer-loop（lease / tick / budget / crash-recovery）の語彙を持つ。\n- **datom-clj** — kotoba Datom-log（EAVT, Datomic-isomorphic）の表現。zero-dep `.cljc`。\n- **actor パターン** — 知能ノードは proposal のみ返し、独立 governor が検閲して可決/拒否。\n  単一不変条件「governor が拒否する書込を actor は決して行わない」。append-only 監査台帳。\n- **楽観 single-entry commit**（ADR-2606272237）— west.yml の pin 前進を tip blob SHA 一致\n  PUT で行い、tip がずれれば 409 で弾く＝conflict が構造的に発生しない経路。\n\n足りないのは **work 分配 + lease の調整層**だけ。本 ADR はそれを定義する。\n\n## Decision\n\n**「kotoba で git をやめる」のではなく「git を末端の materialize 層に降格し、調整を\nkotoba Datom log に引き上げる」。** conflict を解消の対象でなく **発生しない構造**にする。\n\n### 三層で conflict を消す\n\n| 層 | git の挙動 | kotoba の挙動 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **命名** | 単一可変 ref `main` を全員 write | 1 agent = 1 鍵 = 1 IPNS graph。各自の namespace に書く。`main` は派生ビューに降格 |\n| **データ** | ファイル上書き → 行 merge | append-only datom（CID/T）。追記は set-union で単調・決定的 CID。marker が出ない |\n| **commit** | force / 手動 merge | 楽観 single-entry（tip ずれたら 409 → retry）。conflict が構造的に起きない |\n\n### トポロジ\n\n```\n        ┌────────────────── kotoba Datom log (1 論理 log) ──────────────────┐\n        │  append-only / content-addressed / as-of / 両 PC に IPNS+CID 複製   │\n        │  :work/*  :lease/*  :proposal/*  :claim/*  :receipt/*              │\n        └───▲──────────────────────▲───────────────────────────▲───────────┘\n   claim(楽観)│append           append│                    drain │(単一 writer)\n        ┌────┴─────┐         ┌────────┴────────┐         ┌───────┴────────┐\n        │ agent A  │ ...×20  │ agent N         │         │ Governor       │\n        │kotoba-code│        │自分の worktree   │         │ per repo       │\n        │自分の鍵   │        │ or WASM pod     │         │ → git/west pin │\n        └──────────┘         └─────────────────┘         └────────────────┘\n            PC1 ×10                 PC2 ×10                どちらか1台\n   ── murakumo がこの 20 ノードを Tailscale/DID で 1 fleet に畳む ──\n```\n\n### conflict を「起きない」にする 3 仕掛け\n\n1. **Lease で排他（lock サーバ無し）。** 作業単位（repo / module / file-set）を\n   `:lease/*` datom で claim。claim は「append して 409 が返らなければ取得」。20 agent が\n   disjoint な lease を持てば同じファイルに二人触れない。TTL + crash で再 lease。\n2. **提案と materialize の分離（actor 不変条件の転用）。** agent は `:proposal/*`\n   （file write の意図）を追記するだけ。Governor が gate して git に落とす。\n   「governor が拒否する書込を actor は決して行わない」＝ git レベルの race が原理消滅。\n3. **worktree / WASM pod 隔離。** 各 agent は自分の git worktree（or kotoba WASM pod）で\n   編集。FS 衝突ゼロ。merge は `git merge` でなく Datom log + 楽観 commit。\n\n### west との接続\n\n`repos.edn` はそのまま **partition の SSoT**として生きる。変わるのは pin 前進の駆動だけ:\n「人間/各 agent が API を叩く」→「Governor が log の accepted proposal を drain して\nsingle-entry commit（ADR-2606272237 の正経路）する」。`gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` と\n`pin == repo HEAD` の不変条件は維持。既存ガードレールを壊さず上に queue を一段足す。\n\n## 同一ファイル競合の扱い（明示）\n\nlease 粒度を file-set にし、**同一ファイルは同時に 1 lease のみ**を既定にする。どうしても\n共有が必要な構造化資産（EDN/datom 表現）は append-only set-union で自然 merge。非可搬な\nテキスト（コード本体）は lease で直列化し、楽観 claim 競合は 409 → 別 work へ再配分。\n「黙って勝つ」side は作らない（last-writer-wins をコードに適用しない）。\n\n## 足りない 1 ピース = `kotoba-fleet`（仮）coordinator\n\n実装は小さい。**Datom スキーマ + 3 ループ**:\n\n- `:work/*` `:lease/*` `:proposal/*` `:claim/*` `:receipt/*` スキーマ（datom-clj に追加）\n- **claim ループ**（agent 側）: 楽観 lease → kotoba-code 実行 → proposal 追記\n- **governor drain ループ**（repo 単位）: proposal → gate → west single-entry commit → receipt\n- **fleet view**（murakumo 拡張）: 20 lease の TTL / 進捗 / crash 再 lease を 1 view に\n\n新規 actor の標準スキャフォールド（ADR → `.cljc` 正本 → child repo → west 登録 →\nRAD identity）にそのまま乗る。\n\n## Maturity\n\n- **F0** — datom スキーマ（work/lease/proposal/claim/receipt）を datom-clj に定義、contract test。\n- **F1** — claim ループ（楽観 lease + TTL + crash 再 lease）。単一 PC で 2〜3 agent PoC。\n- **F2** — governor drain（proposal → gate → west single-entry commit → receipt）。git 単一 writer。\n- **F3** — worktree / WASM pod 隔離を agent ランタイム（kotoba-code）に統合。\n- **F4** — murakumo fleet view 拡張、2 PC × ~20 agent への横展開、log の IPNS/CID 複製運用。\n\n## Consequences\n\n- git は「末端の materialize 層」に降格し、20 並列 writer を見なくなる（conflict 構造消滅）。\n- 全 agent の turn-history / proposal / receipt が append-only Datom log に載り、\n  resumable・auditable・time-travelable（kotoba-code の as-of がそのまま fleet 監査になる）。\n- 既存の west / repos.edn / 楽観 single-entry commit / murakumo を破壊せず上に積む（後方互換）。\n- 新たな単一障害点は governor だが、repo 単位で分割され lease で隔離されるため局所化される。\n- coordinator 自体が新 child repo + west entry + RAD identity を要する（actor 完了条件）。", :adr/decision "{:thesis \"do not abandon git; demote git to a terminal materialize layer and lift coordination onto the kotoba Datom log; make conflict structurally impossible rather than something to resolve\", :three-layers [{:layer \"naming\", :git \"single mutable ref main, everyone writes\", :kotoba \"1 agent = 1 key = 1 IPNS graph; main demoted to derived view\"} {:layer \"data\", :git \"file overwrite -> line merge\", :kotoba \"append-only datom (CID/T); appends are set-union, monotonic, deterministic CID; no markers\"} {:layer \"commit\", :git \"force / manual merge\", :kotoba \"optimistic single-entry; 409 on stale tip -> retry; no structural conflict\"}], :no-conflict-mechanisms [{:m \"lease exclusion without lock server\", :how \"claim work-unit (repo/module/file-set) via :lease/* datom; claim = append, success if no 409; TTL + crash re-lease\"} {:m \"separate proposal from materialize (actor invariant)\", :how \"agent only appends :proposal/*; governor gates and lands to git; eliminates git-level race\"} {:m \"worktree / WASM-pod isolation\", :how \"each agent edits in its own git worktree or kotoba WASM pod; FS collision zero; merge via Datom log + optimistic commit\"}]}", :adr/topology "{:log \"1 logical kotoba Datom log; append-only; content-addressed; as-of; replicated to both PCs via IPNS+CID\", :namespaces [:work :lease :proposal :claim :receipt], :agents {:count \"~20\", :placement \"PC1 x10, PC2 x10\", :runtime \"kotoba-code, own key, own worktree or WASM pod\"}, :governor {:scope \"per repo\", :role \"single writer; drain accepted proposals -> git/west pin\"}, :fleet-control \"murakumo folds the 20 nodes into 1 view over Tailscale/DID\"}", :adr/substrate-already-present "{:kotoba \"content-addressed distributed datalog; 1 actor = 1 Ed25519 key = key-derived IPNS graph; depth-1 self-mint\", :kotoba-code \"agentic coding agent; persists all turn-history on Datom log as-of => resumable/auditable/fleet-shared checkpointer\", :murakumo \"Mac fleet kotoba WASM mesh control plane; Tailscale/DID 1-view; durable outer-loop lease/tick/budget/crash-recovery\", :datom-clj \"kotoba Datom-log (EAVT, Datomic-isomorphic) representation; zero-dep cljc\", :actor-pattern \"intelligence proposes only; independent governor adjudicates; invariant: actor never does what governor denies; append-only ledger\", :single-entry-commit \"ADR-2606272237; west.yml pin advance by tip-blob-SHA PUT; 409 on stale tip => no structural conflict\", :missing \"work-distribution + lease coordination layer\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"owner request 2026-06-30\", :goal \"2 PCs, ~20 terminal Claude Code agents, parallel/concurrent dev, no conflicts\", :root-cause \"git conflict is a property of shared-mutable ref (main) + line-based 3-way merge, not of parallelism\", :current \"west(repos.edn SSoT, ~50 child repos) + radicle + GitHub; coordination still sits on top of git\"}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2606302000: kotoba Datom log as coordination substrate for 20-agent fleet parallel dev (lease + governor-drain)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]